The `test_put_data_overwrite` test case fails because the `drop` callback is invoked more times than expected. This happens due to an inconsistency in how `mpsc_pbuf_put_data` checks for available space compared to other `put` and `alloc` functions in `mpsc_pbuf.c`.

Specifically, after `mpsc_pbuf_put_data` attempts to free space by dropping an item, it re-evaluates the available `free_wlen`. If `free_wlen` is exactly equal to the `wlen` of the item being put, `mpsc_pbuf_put_data` currently enters the `else` branch (`free_wlen > wlen` is false) and attempts to drop *another* item. This leads to an extra call to the `drop` callback, causing `drop_cnt` to exceed `exp_drop_cnt` and triggering the assertion failure.

Other functions like `mpsc_pbuf_alloc` and `mpsc_pbuf_put_word_ext` correctly use `free_wlen >= wlen` (or `free_wlen >= l`) to determine if enough space is available. The fix is to align `mpsc_pbuf_put_data` with this behavior by changing the condition from `free_wlen > wlen` to `free_wlen >= wlen`.

